extremely|very|ADVERB|To a very high degree|To a very great extent.|cực kỳ; vô cùng|The instructions are extremely detailed.|Hướng dẫn cực kỳ chi tiết.|Degree adverb before gradable adjective.|0
haste|hurry|NOUN|Hurried action|Speed in doing something, often without enough care.|sự vội vã|In her haste, she left the receipt behind.|Vì vội vã, cô ấy bỏ quên hóa đơn.|Uncountable; in haste.|-
escort|accompany|VERB|Accompany to a destination|To accompany someone to guide or protect them on a journey.|hộ tống; đưa đi|An attendant escorted us to our seats.|Một nhân viên đưa chúng tôi đến chỗ ngồi.|Escort someone to somewhere.|-
hazardous|dangerous|ADJECTIVE|Involving danger|Involving a risk of harm.|nguy hiểm|The sign marks a hazardous section of the trail.|Biển báo đánh dấu đoạn đường mòn nguy hiểm.|Hazardous conditions or activity.|-
entice|attract|VERB|Attract with an offer|To persuade someone to do something by offering something appealing.|dụ; lôi cuốn|The discount enticed more visitors into the shop.|Mức giảm giá thu hút thêm khách vào cửa hàng.|Entice someone into doing or to do.|-
